The city tree commission shall have the powers and authority to do the following:
(1) To study and to make determinations and recommendations to the mayor and council regarding the planting, maintenance, and/or protection of trees and shrubs upon public properties and/or in public places;
(2) To make recommendations to the mayor and council of the types, kinds, and species of trees and/or shrubs to be planted upon the right-of-ways of city streets, public parks, and other public facilities or places;
(3) To make recommendations to the mayor and council regarding the removal of any trees and/or shrubs it deems hazardous to the public safety or public health or which, because of disease, fungus, or infestation, are not likely to survive or which may cause such disease, fungus, or infestation to spread;
(4) To identify and to designate any "landmark tree" within the City of Chatsworth. For purposes of this section, a "landmark tree" shall include, but not be limited to, a tree which has particular significance, as evidenced by any one of the following criteria; rare species, large size, estimated age over 50 years, location, unique characteristics, visibility from scenic byway, scenic enhancement, or association with a notable event or person. Designation as a "landmark tree" shall be in the discretion of the commission based upon the foregoing factors, with appeal to the mayor and council. The effect of such designation shall be that landmark trees may not be removed or pruned in any manner which may or could damage the tree, except upon notice and a hearing before the commission and a specific finding therefrom that such tree is then hazardous to the public safety or to the public health and that there is no reasonable alternative to the removal or pruning, as requested;
(5) To assist the city parks and recreation department with the protection and maintenance of existing trees and/or shrubs upon all city owned recreational lands and properties;
(6) To assist the mayor and council and to make available to the general public advice and resource information regarding the selection, planting, and maintenance of trees and/or shrubs, particularly as related to drought tolerance issues;
(7) To make recommendations from time to time regarding proposed ordinances, rules, or requirements of the city relating to the protection and maintenance of trees and/or shrubs within the City of Chatsworth.
(Ord. of 10-1-90, § 3; Ord. of 8-12-2002)

