On or after July 1, 1991, no construction may be initiated within the city for any residential building of any type which:
(1) Employs a gravity tank-type, flushometer-valve, or flushometer-tank toilet that uses more than an average of one and six-tenths gallons of water per flush; provided, however, this paragraph shall not be applicable to one-piece toilets until July 1, 1992;
